WEBVTT
Kind: subtitles
Language: en

1
00:00.200 --> 00:05.860
So one way to make sense of the problems you encounter
is to think about the problem-solving time horizon.

2
00:06.210 --> 00:09.200
And I often think about it in three ways.

3
00:09.200 --> 00:15.600
There's problem solving in the moment. There's problem solving where
you may have a week or two weeks to come to an answer.

4
00:15.600 --> 00:20.380
And there's problem solving over a longer-term project.

5
00:20.610 --> 00:25.200
In each of those cases, there are different aspects
of the problem-solving process that you might want to focus on.

6
00:25.200 --> 00:31.200
So when you're problem solving in the moment, it's really critical to think about:
have you defined the problem and thought about all the constraints in the solution set?

7
00:31.200 --> 00:36.390
You might not have time to formally whip out a sheet of paper
and go through each of the approaches and tools. But the question is:

8
00:37.060 --> 00:41.200
what thinking can you do to really test, in that moment,
have you really defined the problem?

9
00:41.200 --> 00:49.150
Have you aligned all the stakeholders on that? And have you thought about
whether the solution space we're looking at is well scoped?

10
00:49.770 --> 00:55.400
When you're problem solving in one to two weeks, you've got a little more time
to do that analysis — but not a lot of time.

11
00:55.400 --> 01:01.790
There can be more things you probably want to look at
than you have time to do.

12
01:02.120 --> 01:08.400
And really, in that one-to-two-week time horizon, it's thinking about
how you prioritize the issues and analyses you want to conduct.

13
01:08.400 --> 01:16.120
When you're thinking about problem solving in terms of a longer-term project,
you've got more time. But in those cases you probably also have more complexity.

14
01:16.580 --> 01:20.600
There's probably a lot of value at stake. And in those cases,
you want to think about what is the right way to work-plan,

15
01:20.600 --> 01:25.400
and think about: what are the dependencies?
What are the stakeholders you need to align?

16
01:25.400 --> 01:30.840
What decisions do you need to come to early in the process
that may have knock-on effects later in the project's lifespan?
